# Goal Description

The goal is to fix a UI bug where the "GeM Documents" list stays visible underneath the "Custom Declarations" step, and to introduce a new "Final Document Ordering" step. This new step will allow the user to see a line-by-line list of all documents (both AI-mapped standards and custom generated declarations) and rearrange their order before the final merge.

## Proposed Changes

### Frontend (`index.html`)

- **[MODIFY] `index.html`**
  - Fix `showStep3b()` to correctly hide `gemDocsCard` so the screens no longer overlap.
  - Redesign `step4Card` into a "Final Review & Document Ordering" screen.
  - When transitioning to Step 4, dynamically gather all standard selected documents (from Step 1) and all custom generated declarations (from Step 3b).
  - Render them as a list with "Up" and "Down" arrows to allow the user to arrange them exactly how they want them to appear in the final merged PDF.
  - Add a "Remove" button next to each item so users can discard any document at the very last second.
  - Upon clicking "Merge All Documents Now", package this exact order into a new JSON variable (`ordered_docs`) and send it to the backend.

### Backend (`app/api/main.py`)

- **[MODIFY] `main.py` (generate step)**
  - Update the `generate` logic to accept the new `ordered_docs` parameter.
  - Keep the existing generation logic (filling Word docs, converting to PDFs).
  - Instead of blindly appending documents to the final list, store the generated PDFs in a dictionary.
  - Construct the final PDF list to be merged by iterating through the user's `ordered_docs` array, ensuring the final merged PDF strictly respects the user's chosen arrangement.

## Verification Plan

### Manual Verification
1. Map a few documents in Step 1, leaving some blank.
2. Generate a custom declaration in Step 3b.
3. Verify that Step 1 is hidden while in Step 3b.
4. Proceed to Step 4. Verify that the standard documents and the custom declaration appear in a single unified list.
5. Rearrange the list using the UI controls.
6. Click Merge and verify the final downloaded PDF matches the exact order configured in the UI.
